WEBVTT

00:00:00.043 --> 00:00:01.044 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
GridBot Builder.

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:02.784 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
GridBot Blueprint.

00:00:03.349 --> 00:00:04.113 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Lesson two.

00:00:04.633 --> 00:00:06.141 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
What you are going to need.

00:00:06.952 --> 00:00:08.098 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Education only.

00:00:08.657 --> 00:00:09.971 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Not financial advice.

00:00:10.491 --> 00:00:12.542 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This is general information and

00:00:12.542 --> 00:00:14.746 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
doesn't consider your objectives,

00:00:14.746 --> 00:00:16.646 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
financial situation or needs.

00:00:17.166 --> 00:00:18.930 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Crypto is high risk; you could

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:20.621 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
lose all the money you put in.

00:00:21.141 --> 00:00:23.206 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Past performance is not a reliable

00:00:23.206 --> 00:00:24.915 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
indicator of future results.

00:00:25.965 --> 00:00:28.022 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The prices are public historical

00:00:28.022 --> 00:00:29.784 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
daily closes, marked Example.

00:00:30.984 --> 00:00:32.883 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
No order is sent from this lesson.

00:00:33.882 --> 00:00:35.763 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Crypto is a digital coin, such

00:00:35.763 --> 00:00:37.566 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
as bitcoin, and a daily close

00:00:37.566 --> 00:00:39.370 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
is the last price of that day.

00:00:39.890 --> 00:00:41.986 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A band, also called the range, is

00:00:41.986 --> 00:00:43.999 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the top and the bottom, a gap is

00:00:43.999 --> 00:00:46.180 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the space between two lines, and

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:48.276 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the step is how wide that gap is.

00:00:48.796 --> 00:00:50.812 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A stop is the rule for what you will

00:00:50.812 --> 00:00:52.611 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
do if the price leaves the band.

00:00:53.131 --> 00:00:55.031 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Like a packing list before a trip,

00:00:55.031 --> 00:00:56.930 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
your page comes before any screen.

00:00:57.854 --> 00:00:59.474 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
By the end you will fill in a

00:00:59.474 --> 00:01:01.302 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
seven-item checklist on paper.

00:01:02.502 --> 00:01:04.792 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You will keep every secret off that page.

00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:07.644 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You will mark the page Example so

00:01:07.644 --> 00:01:09.376 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
nobody can read it as an order.

00:01:10.484 --> 00:01:12.882 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The seven items are: a notebook, the

00:01:12.882 --> 00:01:15.279 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
three words from lesson one, range,

00:01:15.279 --> 00:01:17.676 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
levels and stop, the pair, paper or a

00:01:17.676 --> 00:01:20.416 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
demo account, no secrets, a written stop,

00:01:20.416 --> 00:01:22.984 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and the word Example on every figure.

00:01:23.504 --> 00:01:24.733 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A pair is what you buy

00:01:24.733 --> 00:01:25.962 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and what you pay with.

00:01:26.455 --> 00:01:27.964 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
For this course the pair is

00:01:27.964 --> 00:01:29.602 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bitcoin priced in US dollars.

00:01:30.122 --> 00:01:32.315 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A demo account uses pretend money.

00:01:32.835 --> 00:01:33.970 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A daily close is the

00:01:33.970 --> 00:01:35.199 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
last price of the day.

00:01:35.696 --> 00:01:37.149 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You are naming that public

00:01:37.149 --> 00:01:38.713 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
series, not choosing an app.

00:01:39.525 --> 00:01:41.256 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Three words, before any number.

00:01:41.662 --> 00:01:44.247 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Range is the top line and the bottom line.

00:01:44.767 --> 00:01:47.133 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Levels are the price lines where orders

00:01:47.133 --> 00:01:49.312 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
wait, like the rungs of a ladder, and a

00:01:49.312 --> 00:01:51.379 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
gap is the space between two of them.

00:01:51.813 --> 00:01:54.159 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A stop is the rule for what you will do if

00:01:54.159 --> 00:01:56.565 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a daily close finishes outside the band

00:01:56.565 --> 00:01:59.051 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and the next daily close is still outside.

00:01:59.571 --> 00:02:01.391 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The figures from lesson 1 are

00:02:01.391 --> 00:02:03.060 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
on the card, marked Example.

00:02:03.580 --> 00:02:05.591 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If you can only say one of the three

00:02:05.591 --> 00:02:07.490 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
words, the page is missing a part.

00:02:08.361 --> 00:02:10.321 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A seed phrase is the list of words

00:02:10.321 --> 00:02:12.065 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
that unlocks a crypto wallet.

00:02:12.585 --> 00:02:14.760 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A private key or an API secret is a

00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:17.015 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
password that can move your money.

00:02:17.535 --> 00:02:20.162 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You never type a seed phrase, a private

00:02:20.162 --> 00:02:22.535 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
key, or an API secret onto this page.

00:02:23.055 --> 00:02:24.854 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The chart has no balance on it.

00:02:25.374 --> 00:02:27.329 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A public close is not your account.

00:02:27.804 --> 00:02:29.435 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If a form asks for a secret,

00:02:29.435 --> 00:02:31.221 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
that form is not this lesson.

00:02:32.271 --> 00:02:33.841 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You copy the band onto the

00:02:33.841 --> 00:02:35.562 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
page, not every day's prices.

00:02:36.082 --> 00:02:38.316 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Copy the bottom line and the top

00:02:38.316 --> 00:02:40.464 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
line, with six gaps of about 900.

00:02:40.984 --> 00:02:42.436 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Every close in that window

00:02:42.436 --> 00:02:43.721 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
stayed inside the band.

00:02:44.266 --> 00:02:45.668 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Mark each figure Example.

00:02:46.718 --> 00:02:48.258 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Worked check: pair, band,

00:02:48.258 --> 00:02:49.716 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
gaps, stop, and Example.

00:02:50.236 --> 00:02:52.303 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If the stop line is only a tick with

00:02:52.303 --> 00:02:54.517 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
no sentence, the page fails the check.

00:02:55.037 --> 00:02:56.810 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The rule has to say: if a daily

00:02:56.810 --> 00:02:58.891 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
close finishes outside the band

00:02:58.891 --> 00:03:00.973 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and the next daily close is still

00:03:00.973 --> 00:03:02.746 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
outside, the example is over.

00:03:03.796 --> 00:03:05.807 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A page is the notebook you can hold.

00:03:06.302 --> 00:03:07.811 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The screen is the exchange.

00:03:08.241 --> 00:03:09.764 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Lesson 1 ended by asking

00:03:09.764 --> 00:03:11.059 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
you to bring the page.

00:03:11.579 --> 00:03:12.975 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This lesson is that page.

00:03:14.020 --> 00:03:16.087 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Write today's date on the first line.

00:03:16.437 --> 00:03:18.280 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Under it, write the word Example.

00:03:18.664 --> 00:03:20.142 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Example means a real past

00:03:20.142 --> 00:03:21.551 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
price used for practice.

00:03:22.071 --> 00:03:24.194 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It is not an order and not a forecast.

00:03:25.224 --> 00:03:26.509 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The seven items are the

00:03:26.509 --> 00:03:27.738 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
list you can point at.

00:03:28.318 --> 00:03:29.068 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A notebook.

00:03:29.369 --> 00:03:31.230 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The three words from lesson one,

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:33.090 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
which are range, levels and stop.

00:03:33.816 --> 00:03:34.566 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The pair.

00:03:34.743 --> 00:03:35.874 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Paper or a demo.

00:03:36.452 --> 00:03:37.354 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
No secrets.

00:03:38.088 --> 00:03:38.926 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A written stop.

00:03:39.298 --> 00:03:41.167 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The word Example on every figure.

00:03:42.312 --> 00:03:43.485 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Write the pair first.

00:03:43.889 --> 00:03:45.615 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
For this course it is bitcoin

00:03:45.615 --> 00:03:46.837 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
priced in US dollars.

00:03:47.357 --> 00:03:49.033 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Every other row depends on it.

00:03:49.375 --> 00:03:51.551 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If a fee sum is in Australian

00:03:51.551 --> 00:03:53.727 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
dollars, that sum goes on its

00:03:53.727 --> 00:03:55.808 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
own line, labelled BTC/AUD.

00:03:56.328 --> 00:03:58.387 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Do not put a US dollar price and an

00:03:58.387 --> 00:04:00.750 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Australian dollar fee on the same row.

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:04.385 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Range is the top line and the bottom line.

00:04:04.905 --> 00:04:06.869 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
On the summer chart those lines are

00:04:06.869 --> 00:04:08.712 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the bottom line and the top line.

00:04:09.149 --> 00:04:10.546 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Both figures are Example.

00:04:11.049 --> 00:04:12.948 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Levels are the lines between them.

00:04:13.239 --> 00:04:15.397 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Six gaps of about 900 dollars sit

00:04:15.397 --> 00:04:17.396 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
between the top and the bottom.

00:04:18.446 --> 00:04:19.858 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The stop sentence has to

00:04:19.858 --> 00:04:21.031 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
say what you will do.

00:04:21.507 --> 00:04:23.518 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Two daily closes outside the band,

00:04:23.518 --> 00:04:25.458 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
through the top or the bottom, and

00:04:25.458 --> 00:04:27.325 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the second close still outside.

00:04:27.845 --> 00:04:29.410 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then you stop the bot, which

00:04:29.410 --> 00:04:31.208 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
cancels the waiting orders, and

00:04:31.208 --> 00:04:32.889 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
you follow the rule you wrote.

00:04:33.939 --> 00:04:35.955 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
An exchange in Australia asks who

00:04:35.955 --> 00:04:37.755 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
you are before you can deposit.

00:04:38.275 --> 00:04:40.174 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
That check is the exchange's rule.

00:04:40.469 --> 00:04:42.473 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You only upload identification

00:04:42.473 --> 00:04:44.328 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
inside the exchange's own app.

00:04:44.848 --> 00:04:46.915 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This course does not name an exchange

00:04:46.915 --> 00:04:48.479 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and does not show a balance.

00:04:49.270 --> 00:04:50.858 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Before you deposit, look the

00:04:50.858 --> 00:04:52.861 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
exchange up on the public register.

00:04:53.381 --> 00:04:55.671 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The register says the business is listed.

00:04:56.098 --> 00:04:58.333 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It does not say your money is protected.

00:04:59.142 --> 00:05:00.818 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A second code, as well as your

00:05:00.818 --> 00:05:03.257 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
password, is two-factor authentication.

00:05:03.777 --> 00:05:05.877 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Turn that on before any real dollars.

00:05:06.397 --> 00:05:08.430 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then look for a paper or demo mode.

00:05:09.016 --> 00:05:10.538 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Paper uses pretend money.

00:05:11.058 --> 00:05:12.678 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
That practice is lesson 7.

00:05:13.728 --> 00:05:16.019 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A maker fee is the charge when your order

00:05:16.019 --> 00:05:18.141 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
waits and someone else trades with it.

00:05:18.351 --> 00:05:20.027 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A taker fee is the charge when

00:05:20.027 --> 00:05:21.759 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
your order fills straight away.

00:05:22.096 --> 00:05:23.794 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A grid uses waiting orders,

00:05:23.794 --> 00:05:25.493 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
so read the maker fee first.

00:05:26.013 --> 00:05:28.835 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
In this example both are 0.1 percent.

00:05:29.885 --> 00:05:32.965 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
On an example buy of 100 Australian

00:05:32.965 --> 00:05:35.726 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
dollars, 0.1 percent is 10 cents.

00:05:36.246 --> 00:05:38.369 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The sell costs about 10 cents as well.

00:05:38.690 --> 00:05:40.534 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The round trip is about 20

00:05:40.534 --> 00:05:42.466 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
cents, which is 0.2 percent.

00:05:42.986 --> 00:05:45.024 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This fee row is Australian dollars.

00:05:45.544 --> 00:05:47.499 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It is not the summer bitcoin price.

00:05:48.425 --> 00:05:50.391 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If the gap is smaller than that

00:05:50.391 --> 00:05:52.357 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
0.2 percent, the pair loses the

00:05:52.357 --> 00:05:54.087 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
fee before the price moves.

00:05:54.607 --> 00:05:56.151 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Lesson 5 is where you test

00:05:56.151 --> 00:05:57.475 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a gap against this fee.

00:05:57.995 --> 00:06:00.062 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You do not pick a gap in this lesson.

00:06:00.695 --> 00:06:02.854 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A journal is the page you will open

00:06:02.854 --> 00:06:04.782 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
again in lesson 8 and lesson 10.

00:06:05.302 --> 00:06:07.356 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
For every buy, sell or swap, write

00:06:07.356 --> 00:06:09.410 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the date and time, the amount, the

00:06:09.410 --> 00:06:11.701 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
value in Australian dollars at the

00:06:11.701 --> 00:06:13.676 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
time, the fee, which exchange or

00:06:13.676 --> 00:06:15.809 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
wallet, and what the trade was for.

00:06:16.329 --> 00:06:17.602 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Export that history at

00:06:17.602 --> 00:06:19.009 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
least every three months.

00:06:19.529 --> 00:06:21.301 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This is general information,

00:06:21.301 --> 00:06:22.187 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
not tax advice.

00:06:23.237 --> 00:06:25.025 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Leave two columns blank for now.

00:06:25.444 --> 00:06:26.607 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
One is for the fees.

00:06:27.127 --> 00:06:29.418 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
One is for whether you followed the rule.

00:06:29.552 --> 00:06:30.725 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You fill those later.

00:06:31.174 --> 00:06:33.018 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You do not fill them with a hope.

00:06:33.679 --> 00:06:36.165 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A seed phrase, a private key, or an API

00:06:36.165 --> 00:06:38.822 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
secret unlocks a wallet or an account.

00:06:39.342 --> 00:06:41.633 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Nobody from this course will ask for one.

00:06:42.009 --> 00:06:43.907 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If a message rushes you to send

00:06:43.907 --> 00:06:45.425 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
crypto, treat it as a scam.

00:06:45.945 --> 00:06:47.367 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Moneysmart is the public

00:06:47.367 --> 00:06:49.331 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Australian guide for that warning.

00:06:49.852 --> 00:06:50.858 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Check it yourself.

00:06:51.318 --> 00:06:53.106 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Do not read a web address aloud.

00:06:53.986 --> 00:06:55.662 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Read the page once, out loud.

00:06:56.182 --> 00:06:58.302 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If a word on it has not been defined,

00:06:58.302 --> 00:07:00.422 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
stop and define it before you go on.

00:07:00.988 --> 00:07:02.329 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then close the notebook.

00:07:02.692 --> 00:07:04.168 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The next lesson shows what

00:07:04.168 --> 00:07:05.788 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the bot does, order by order.

00:07:06.694 --> 00:07:08.761 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Say the page once, in your own words,

00:07:08.761 --> 00:07:10.549 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and do not read the chart again.

00:07:10.799 --> 00:07:12.699 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Name the pair, the band, the gaps,

00:07:12.699 --> 00:07:14.369 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and the stop rule, then stop.

00:07:14.889 --> 00:07:16.811 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A secret is a seed phrase, a

00:07:16.811 --> 00:07:18.915 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
private key, or an API secret.

00:07:19.435 --> 00:07:21.111 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
None of those go on this page.

00:07:21.510 --> 00:07:23.188 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You write Example on your own

00:07:23.188 --> 00:07:25.076 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
notebook so a practice sketch is

00:07:25.076 --> 00:07:27.173 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
never later mistaken for a live plan.

00:07:28.223 --> 00:07:30.603 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Recap: your page has seven items, each

00:07:30.603 --> 00:07:32.744 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
with a written fact, every figure

00:07:32.744 --> 00:07:35.044 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
marked Example, and no secrets on it.

00:07:36.244 --> 00:07:38.581 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
An exchange in Australia has to confirm

00:07:38.581 --> 00:07:40.563 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
who you are before you can deposit.

00:07:41.083 --> 00:07:43.017 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
That identity check is the first

00:07:43.017 --> 00:07:44.737 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
step, and it is the exchange's

00:07:44.737 --> 00:07:46.098 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
rule, not this course's.

00:07:47.148 --> 00:07:49.517 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Australian exchanges register with

00:07:49.517 --> 00:07:51.809 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
AUSTRAC, the government agency that

00:07:51.809 --> 00:07:54.025 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
keeps the list of crypto exchanges,

00:07:54.025 --> 00:07:56.317 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
as virtual asset service providers.

00:07:56.837 --> 00:07:59.016 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Check that register before you sign up.

00:07:59.489 --> 00:08:02.084 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Registration is not a safety guarantee.

00:08:02.604 --> 00:08:04.595 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
ASIC is the Australian companies

00:08:04.595 --> 00:08:05.946 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and markets regulator.

00:08:06.466 --> 00:08:09.106 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Its licensing of exchanges

00:08:09.106 --> 00:08:11.172 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
starts on 9 April 2027.

00:08:11.692 --> 00:08:13.653 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This lesson names the regulators

00:08:13.653 --> 00:08:14.994 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
only, never an exchange.

00:08:16.034 --> 00:08:17.374 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Turn on a second code as

00:08:17.374 --> 00:08:18.603 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
well as your password.

00:08:19.082 --> 00:08:21.591 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
That second code is

00:08:21.591 --> 00:08:23.044 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
two-factor authentication.

00:08:23.044 --> 00:08:24.664 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then look for a paper or demo

00:08:24.664 --> 00:08:26.284 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
mode before any real dollars.

00:08:26.903 --> 00:08:28.878 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A pair such as BTC/AUD means

00:08:28.878 --> 00:08:30.938 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
you buy the base, bitcoin, with

00:08:30.938 --> 00:08:33.085 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the quote, Australian dollars.

00:08:33.605 --> 00:08:35.737 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A stablecoin is a coin designed

00:08:35.737 --> 00:08:37.459 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
to stay near one US dollar.

00:08:38.509 --> 00:08:39.971 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A maker fee is the charge

00:08:39.971 --> 00:08:41.360 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
for an order that waits.

00:08:41.880 --> 00:08:43.668 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A taker fee is the charge for an

00:08:43.668 --> 00:08:45.400 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
order that fills straight away.

00:08:45.724 --> 00:08:48.547 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
In this example both are 0.1 percent.

00:08:49.597 --> 00:08:52.677 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
On an example buy of 100 Australian

00:08:52.677 --> 00:08:55.438 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
dollars, 0.1 percent is 10 cents.

00:08:55.958 --> 00:08:58.080 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The sell costs about 10 cents as well.

00:08:58.402 --> 00:09:00.246 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The round trip is about 20

00:09:00.246 --> 00:09:02.178 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
cents, which is 0.2 percent.

00:09:03.228 --> 00:09:05.139 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Any gap smaller than that 0.2

00:09:05.139 --> 00:09:06.971 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
percent loses money before

00:09:06.971 --> 00:09:08.564 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the price does anything.

00:09:09.084 --> 00:09:10.861 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Lesson 5 uses this as the

00:09:10.861 --> 00:09:12.372 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
test a gap has to pass.

00:09:13.422 --> 00:09:15.171 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A trading journal is a dated

00:09:15.171 --> 00:09:17.148 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
record of every bot: the plan, the

00:09:17.148 --> 00:09:18.897 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
changes, the fills, the fees, a

00:09:18.897 --> 00:09:20.950 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
review note of what happened, and

00:09:20.950 --> 00:09:22.927 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
whether you followed the rules.

00:09:23.447 --> 00:09:25.235 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
That note is not money you made.

00:09:26.113 --> 00:09:28.450 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The columns are the date, the pair, the

00:09:28.450 --> 00:09:30.787 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
band, the gaps, the money in the bot, the

00:09:30.787 --> 00:09:33.202 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
stop rule, the fills, the pairs, the fees,

00:09:33.202 --> 00:09:35.617 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the result, and a yes or no for the rules.

00:09:36.667 --> 00:09:38.980 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The summer band on the card is a

00:09:38.980 --> 00:09:41.663 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bitcoin price in US dollars, so that

00:09:41.663 --> 00:09:44.161 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
example row is labelled BTC/USD.

00:09:44.681 --> 00:09:47.519 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The fee example in Australian dollars

00:09:47.519 --> 00:09:50.091 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
is a separate row, labelled BTC/AUD.

00:09:50.611 --> 00:09:52.901 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Do not mix the two currencies on one row.

00:09:53.897 --> 00:09:55.897 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Nobody from this course will

00:09:55.897 --> 00:09:57.396 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
ask for a seed phrase, a

00:09:57.396 --> 00:09:59.313 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
private key, or an API secret.

00:09:59.833 --> 00:10:01.856 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Those are the secret words or keys

00:10:01.856 --> 00:10:03.735 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
that unlock a wallet or account.

00:10:04.785 --> 00:10:06.683 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If a message rushes you to send

00:10:06.683 --> 00:10:08.202 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
crypto, treat it as a scam.

00:10:08.722 --> 00:10:10.361 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Moneysmart is the Australian

00:10:10.361 --> 00:10:11.646 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
guide for that warning.

00:10:12.126 --> 00:10:13.011 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This is general

00:10:13.011 --> 00:10:14.519 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
information, not a product.

00:10:15.557 --> 00:10:16.898 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Write the seven items as

00:10:16.898 --> 00:10:18.239 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a list you can point at.

00:10:19.505 --> 00:10:20.255 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A notebook.

00:10:21.236 --> 00:10:22.688 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The three words, which are

00:10:22.688 --> 00:10:23.973 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
range, levels and stop.

00:10:25.338 --> 00:10:26.088 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The pair.

00:10:26.945 --> 00:10:28.077 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Paper or a demo.

00:10:29.334 --> 00:10:30.237 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
No secrets.

00:10:31.651 --> 00:10:32.489 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A written stop.

00:10:33.541 --> 00:10:35.410 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The word Example on every figure.

00:10:36.610 --> 00:10:37.990 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Each item has a reason.

00:10:39.190 --> 00:10:40.531 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The notebook is the plan

00:10:40.531 --> 00:10:41.648 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
you can check later.

00:10:42.581 --> 00:10:43.922 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The three words stop you

00:10:43.922 --> 00:10:45.542 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
drawing a grid with no edges.

00:10:46.592 --> 00:10:47.876 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The pair names what you

00:10:47.876 --> 00:10:49.329 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
buy and what you pay with.

00:10:50.383 --> 00:10:52.410 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Paper or a demo is the L-plate.

00:10:53.610 --> 00:10:55.788 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
No secrets keeps the keys off the page.

00:10:56.961 --> 00:10:58.693 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The written stop is the action.

00:10:59.666 --> 00:11:01.454 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Example marks a teaching number.

00:11:02.544 --> 00:11:04.500 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A maker fee is paid when your order

00:11:04.500 --> 00:11:06.622 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
waits and someone else trades with it.

00:11:07.484 --> 00:11:09.104 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A taker fee is paid when your

00:11:09.104 --> 00:11:10.557 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
order fills straight away.

00:11:11.471 --> 00:11:13.657 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A grid uses waiting orders, so the

00:11:13.657 --> 00:11:15.843 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
maker fee is the one to read first.

00:11:17.043 --> 00:11:18.663 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The round trip is both sides.

00:11:19.811 --> 00:11:22.914 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
On the example of 100 Australian dollars

00:11:22.914 --> 00:11:25.926 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
at 0.1 percent each side, the buy costs 10

00:11:25.926 --> 00:11:28.846 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
cents and the sell costs about 10 cents.

00:11:29.896 --> 00:11:32.229 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Twenty cents is 0.2 percent.

00:11:33.429 --> 00:11:35.440 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If the gap is smaller than that, the

00:11:35.440 --> 00:11:37.340 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
pair loses before the price moves.

00:11:38.309 --> 00:11:39.888 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
That is why lesson 5 tests

00:11:39.888 --> 00:11:41.316 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the gap against the fee.

00:11:42.516 --> 00:11:44.450 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The journal is the page you will

00:11:44.450 --> 00:11:46.235 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
open in lesson 8 and lesson 10.

00:11:47.435 --> 00:11:49.488 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
For every buy, sell or swap write

00:11:49.488 --> 00:11:51.542 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the date and time, the amount, the

00:11:51.542 --> 00:11:53.833 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
value in Australian dollars at the

00:11:53.833 --> 00:11:55.808 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
time, the fee, which exchange or

00:11:55.808 --> 00:11:57.467 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
wallet, and what it was for.

00:11:58.517 --> 00:11:59.696 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Export the history at

00:11:59.696 --> 00:12:01.092 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
least every three months.

00:12:02.271 --> 00:12:04.043 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This is general information,

00:12:04.043 --> 00:12:04.929 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
not tax advice.

00:12:06.129 --> 00:12:07.950 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If a message asks for a seed

00:12:07.950 --> 00:12:09.936 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
phrase, a private key, or an API

00:12:09.936 --> 00:12:11.839 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
secret, it is not this course.

00:12:13.039 --> 00:12:15.385 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Those words unlock a wallet or an account.

00:12:16.490 --> 00:12:18.693 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Moneysmart is the public Australian

00:12:18.693 --> 00:12:20.114 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
guide for scam warnings.

00:12:21.314 --> 00:12:23.102 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Do not read a web address aloud.

00:12:24.170 --> 00:12:25.734 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Check the register yourself.

00:12:26.861 --> 00:12:28.872 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Open the notebook before any screen.

00:12:29.933 --> 00:12:31.561 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Write today's date at the top

00:12:31.561 --> 00:12:33.237 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and the word Example under it.

00:12:34.388 --> 00:12:36.176 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Write the pair on the next line.

00:12:37.121 --> 00:12:40.236 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If the prices are the summer

00:12:40.241 --> 00:12:41.917 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bitcoin closes, write BTC/USD.

00:12:42.629 --> 00:12:45.015 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If the fee sum is in Australian

00:12:45.015 --> 00:12:47.973 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
dollars, write BTC/AUD on its own line.

00:12:49.173 --> 00:12:51.029 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Write the top and the bottom only

00:12:51.029 --> 00:12:53.040 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
after you have said what a range is.

00:12:54.153 --> 00:12:56.043 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then write one gap, and how you

00:12:56.043 --> 00:12:58.012 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
got it: the top minus the bottom,

00:12:58.012 --> 00:12:59.901 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
divided by the number of gaps.

00:13:01.101 --> 00:13:03.562 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Write the stop in one sentence: two daily

00:13:03.562 --> 00:13:06.023 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
closes outside, then you stop the bot and

00:13:06.023 --> 00:13:08.112 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
follow the rule you already chose.

00:13:09.312 --> 00:13:11.602 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Leave a blank column for fees and a blank

00:13:11.602 --> 00:13:13.893 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
column for whether you followed the rule.

00:13:14.806 --> 00:13:15.980 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You fill those later.

00:13:17.108 --> 00:13:18.952 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You do not fill them with a hope.

00:13:19.763 --> 00:13:21.251 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Read the page aloud once.

00:13:22.451 --> 00:13:24.571 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If a word on it has not been defined,

00:13:24.571 --> 00:13:26.691 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
stop and define it before you go on.

00:13:27.891 --> 00:13:29.873 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Next lesson: What is a grid bot.

00:13:30.393 --> 00:13:31.958 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Bring your notes: your band,

00:13:31.958 --> 00:13:33.578 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
your gaps and your stop rule.

00:13:33.851 --> 00:13:35.208 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Keep the word Example on

00:13:35.208 --> 00:13:36.498 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
every practice figure.

00:13:37.018 --> 00:13:38.666 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Next lesson you will see what

00:13:38.666 --> 00:13:40.286 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the bot does, order by order.

